{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the mixed swarm departed.</b> It does not say 'and the mixed swarm died,' as it said of the frogs, ״וימותו הצפרדעים״, because the intent of the Holy One, blessed be He, in the plagues was to torment them and embitter their lives, not to bring them any benefit. Therefore He needed to kill the frogs among them, so that it would be a torment to them. And so Moshe said in his words concerning the extermination of the frogs — and extermination is death; and even though it says ״וסרו הצפרדעים״, the meaning is that through their extermination and death the plague departs from them. But the mixed swarm needed to return to their places, to their haunts, as they came from there — not to exterminate and kill them among them, for this would bring them benefit, and the Master of all, blessed be He, did not intend that."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:06.553749507Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}